"""sympsica's ZT-4 part (b) driver — task-7-brief.md, W2.3 Test C.

A minimal, self-contained bzlmod workspace (separate from the CMake project
that builds the rest of sympsica): its only purpose is to link
oracle_check.cc against the vendored, SHA-pinned
google/distributed_point_functions checkout (../../../../vendor/
distributed_point_functions — see PINS.md for the pinned SHA and the exact
host-toolchain pins this required) and run it as `bazel test`.

Build: from this directory,
  USE_BAZEL_VERSION=7.4.1 bazelisk test --copt=-DHWY_DISABLED_TARGETS=25952256 //:oracle_check
See task-7-report.md for why both pins are required on this host (macOS/ARM):
Bazel 7.4.1 (native cc_proto_library was removed in Bazel 9, and the vendored
dpf/BUILD never gained the explicit @com_google_protobuf//bazel:
cc_proto_library.bzl load some other consumer would need); and
HWY_DISABLED_TARGETS=25952256 (= HWY_SVE2_128|HWY_SVE_256|HWY_SVE2|HWY_SVE)
disables highway's SVE/SVE2 dispatch targets, which Apple Silicon does not
implement and whose HWY_ALIGN(8) is narrower than absl::uint128's required
16-byte alignment on this toolchain.

CAUTION (task-7-report.md, "Correction" section, fix round 1): running
`bazelisk build`/`test` directly against ../../../../vendor/
distributed_point_functions/ itself (not just this workspace) rewrites
THAT checkout's own MODULE.bazel.lock to match whatever subset of the
module graph the invoked target(s) resolved -- on every Bazel version and
every host, not only this one. If you need that checkout's `git status` to
read clean afterward, restore it with `git checkout -- MODULE.bazel.lock`
(never a manual backup/restore -- a backup taken after ANY prior bazel
invocation is already contaminated) before treating its status as evidence
of anything.
"""

module(
    name = "sympsica_zt4_google_dpf_check",
    version = "0.0.0",
)

bazel_dep(name = "distributed_point_functions", version = "0.0.0")
local_path_override(
    module_name = "distributed_point_functions",
    path = "../../../../vendor/distributed_point_functions",
)

bazel_dep(name = "abseil-cpp", version = "20240722.0", repo_name = "com_google_absl")
